word MajorTopicYN="N">food intake</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">leptin-conjugated saporin</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">nucleus of the solitary tract</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">phosphorylated STAT3</Keyword><Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">ventromedial nucleus of the hypothalamus</Keyword></KeywordList><CoiStatement>No conflicts of interest, financial or otherwise, are declared by the authors.</CoiStatement></MedlineCitation><PubmedData><History><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pubmed"><Year>2020</Year><Month>4</Month><Day>2</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>0</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="medline"><Year>2020</Year><Month>7</Month><Day>30</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>0</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="entrez"><Year>2020</Year><Month>4</Month><Day>2</Day><Hour>6</Hour><Minute>0</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pmc-release"><Year>2021</Year><Month>5</Month><Day>1</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">32228323</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC7272723</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1152/ajpendo.00020.2020</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation>Balogh Z, F&#xf3;ris G, Koszt&#xe1;czky B, Paragh G Jr, Seres I, Zs&#xed;ros E, K&#xf3;nya G, Paragh G. The concentration dependent biphasic effect of leptin on endogenous cholesterol synthesis in human monocytes. Peptides 28: 2081&#x2013;2083, 2007. doi: 10.1016/j.peptides.2007.07.004.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.peptides.2007.07.004</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">17875346</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Barrichon M, Hadi T, Wendremaire M, Ptasinski C, Seigneuric R, Marcion G, Delignette M, Marchet J, Dumas M, Sagot P, Bardou M, Garrido C, Lirussi F. Dose-dependent biphasic leptin-induced proliferation is caused by non-specific IL-6/NF-&#x3ba;B pathway activation in human myometrial cells. Br J Pharma