siol Endocrinol Metab 311: E939&#x2013;E948, 2016. doi: 10.1152/ajpendo.00343.2016.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1152/ajpendo.00343.2016</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5183885</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27802966</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Harris RB. Low-dose leptin infusion in the fourth ventricle of rats enhances the response to third-ventricle leptin injection. Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab 313: E134&#x2013;E147, 2017. doi: 10.1152/ajpendo.00052.2017.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1152/ajpendo.00052.2017</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6109645</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28442484</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Harris RB. Low-dose infusions of leptin into the nucleus of the solitary tract increase sensitivity to third ventricle leptin. Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab 316: E719&#x2013;E728, 2019. doi: 10.1152/ajpendo.00562.2018.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1152/ajpendo.00562.2018</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6580178</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30721096</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Herbert H, Moga MM, Saper CB. Connections of the parabrachial nucleus with the nucleus of the solitary tract and the medullary reticular formation in the rat. J Comp Neurol 293: 540&#x2013;580, 1990. doi: 10.1002/cne.902930404.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1002/cne.902930404</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">1691748</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hosoi T, Kawagishi T, Okuma Y, Tanaka J, Nomura Y. Brain stem is a direct target for leptin&#x2019;s action in the central nervous system. Endocrinology 143: 3498&#x2013;3504, 2002. doi: 10.1210/en.2002-220077.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1210/en.2002-220077</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12193563</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citat